Is anyone else having problems running out of memory on their alpha?

I have an Alpha 3000/300 with 64 Meg of RAM and a swap file that is 
"bigger than I'll ever need."  I am trying to port some code from
a SPARC system which has been running there and on PCs for some months.
It was written to be portable between PC - SPARC - Macintosh - DEC Alpha.
The original author of this piece of the code uses recursive makefiles
which seem to be the problem.  Whenever I run the toplevel make, I get 
the out of memory error and a message to try again later.  I'm the only 
one on the machine at the time and I have only a few windows open, but that shouldn't be the problem, virtual memory should take care of this!

I have a workaround - manually run the makes in each subdirectory, but 
this gets old real fast.  BTW, I'm using g++/gcc 2.6.0.

Any ideas?  I'll post a summary of the replies in a few days.


