A few weeks ago, I submitted a series of questions on DECwindows 
customizations and a number of people have asked for a summary.  Here's what I 
have learned. 
 
1.  Eliminate the Digital logo from the login screen ... preferably be able
    to replace the logo, but eliminating it would serve (I know how to 
    eliminate it under ULTRIX but can find no corresponding method under VMS).

    Under VMS, the way to eliminate the logo is:

       $ DEFINE/SYSTEM$ DEFINE/SYS/EXEC DECW$LOGIN_BACKGROUND NL:

    One person responded that in VMS V5.3, DECwindows V2.0, there will be the
    capability to specify and image file name to replace the logo.

    Under ULTRIX, the logo may be turned off in the system .Xdefaults file.
    However, this results in a 15-30 second performance penalty during login.
 
2.  Change the default geometry of the Icon Box.  Also the ability to change
    the default geometry of the Bookreader index window.

    The file DECW$Xdefaults.Dat may be created in your default directory.  The
    resource wm*geometry may be customized to whatever dimensions you want.
    I like my Icon Box in the upper right corner and so I use:

       wm*geometry:                    =250x250+750+1

    (It seems that it may also be placed into DECW$WINMGR.DAT but I haven't
    tried this).

    The same may be done under ULTRIX in your default directory's .Xdefaults
    file.

    For the bookreader in particular, I have learned no information.  Since it
    is not available under ULTRIX, there seems to be no documentation.

 
3.  Completely change the "pause" screen.  What I'd really like is the mouse
    locked to a small password window with the other windows remaining 
    visible.

    I've received no suggestions on this.  A different way to do what I want 
    to might be if there is a positive answer to the question:
    "Under X11, is there such a color as 'transparent'?"

      
4.  A custom background image.

    It seems there is no direct way to do this under VMS.  Opening a window
    to an ULTRIX system and using an ULTRIX window manager instead of the
    VMS DECwindows manager does work but is cumbersome.

    I did get some references to a DECUS version of XSETROOT for VMS but have
    not obtained that and cannot test it.

 
5.  A custom screensaver.

    No information on this one either.

 
>I've searched through the documentation I can find as well as the DECW$*.DAT 
