save it's core image to a file (similar to what gcore(1) does), kill
the original process, and then later (like, say, after rebooting)
restart the process from the saved core image.

I am perfectly willing to write a program to do this, I don't expect
utilities to already to exist, I'm just looking for pointers.

I had though ptrace(2) might could be used, although it would be slow since
you must make a system call for every 4 bytes you read from the process's
address space.  However, I haven't been able to ptrace anything other than
a child of the calling process (ie, the process calling ptrace).

Things that would help would be: source to gcore(1), source to dbx, or
(obviously) source for a utility which does exactly what I am wanting.
(Or, just tell me how to do it, and I'll take care of the details. :-)

Pointers to commercial products would be helpful too, especially if they
are available for DEC/Ultrix (including DECStations) machines.

