In article <12001@watcgl.waterloo.edu>, idallen@watcgl.waterloo.edu writes:
> From: "Ian! D. Allen [CGL]" <idallen>
> 
> On an 8-Meg VAXstation 3100 running Ultrix 3.0 I created a 10Meg file and
> then did:
> 
>     # time dd if=in of=out bs=1024k
> 
> The rz23 took about a minute of real time.  The rz55 consistently 
> took 10-15 seconds longer.
> Why?  

	As shipped the RZ23 has a read-ahead cache which is enabled.
	The RZ55 also has a read-ahead cache, but it isn't enabled.
	Hopefully a future version of rzdisk(8) will support turning
	on the read-ahead cache of the RZ55.  Till then, I don't
