In article <18817@mimsy.UUCP> steve@umiacs.umd.edu (Steve D. Miller) writes:
>
>   I hear a rumor from someone that the DECstation 2100 has no serial
>ports (other than those for the keyboard and mouse, and opposed to the
>3100, which has two additional ports).  Could someone take a look at the
>back of their machine and let me know?
>
>	-Steve

Steve,

The 2100 is exactly the same as the 3100 except for a slower
CPU/FPU (12.5 MHz vs 16.67MHz) and slower cache (35ns vs 23ns).
Other than that, everything is exactly the same; same board etch;
same other components; and same serial ports.  The software was
not redone; they run exactly the same binaries, both user and kernel.

