I have seen problems with Wren V's on the DS3100.
The problem is that the Wren does a seek, disconnects,
and never reselects the initiator (in this case the 3100).
Various people I have talked with are looking into getting
a microcode fix from CDC. At one point I was told that
microcode 5466 worked correctly with "fast machines"
but this does not appear to be accurate. The problem appears
quite readily when using the Wren in synchronous mode with
the cache enable bit turned on (maximum performance mode).
