Just to add my own two cents worth, something that bit us on this was the
way you form the image name when you run the file.  If you specify an explicit
version number on the filename, even if it is the correct one that matches
the known file entry, then the system will not open the file using the known
file entry information, which means among other things that you won't get
the elevated priveleges when you run the program.  We found this because an
overly-helpful menu program tried to use fully qualified file names when
running images, and it disabled privileges, sharing, etc.

Hope this helps.

Tom Cole
SAS Institute

