>Also, is there some way to eliminate all the duplication in the server disk for 
>all the diskless clients? It would be ideal to be able to stick all the custom
>stuff, and /usr/users files on the swap disks. Can this be done? Is it a good
>idea?

It's not hard to do this, though it's not a "supported" configuration.
Generate a kernel with the disk device driver and boot it.  Make a root
filesystem on the local disk (newfs /dev/rrz?a rz??) and dump the current
root to it.  Generate a new kernel that expects its root on the disk, and
install that as vmunix in your new root filesystem.  Reboot and enjoy.

I'd advise leaving /usr/users on a central machine; it's much easier to
administer and back up that way.

