If you have access to a VAX780 or a VAX785 (running VMS) you should be able to
read it. Both of these machines are booted by a LSI-11 that has an eight inch
floppy disk on it.

You will need physical access to the machine as the floppy is only reachable 
once the front doors are open.

The LSI-11 runs RT-11, but if you 'mount' the floppy you have access to it
from VMS. Mounting the floppy requires that a CONNECT CONSOLE is done some
where in the system startup or by someone with the right privs.

Once this has been done then the floppy is available as CSA1:

You can then run the EXCHANGE program to dir directories, copy files to and 
from the floppy, etc.
