You need to set something special in the start up to get it to autoboot,
Not sure what parameter that is but Dec support will know.

Once you've got that set, then you need to tell the VS that there is a
'real' terminal out there.  You need DEC part # BCC08-10 which plugs into
the printer port on the system box.  You don't actually have to have a
terminal on the other end.  The box senses the pins and assumes a live
terminal.  We do it here (hooking up a pc to the printer port and booting)

good hunting (BCC08-10 is about $30 from decdirect)

