> Payment in cash or DECtapes.

This (a) is the wrong part #, and (b) won't solve your problem anyway unless
you have an RX11 (M7846) floppy controller module.  There are two different
floppy boot ROMs for the M9312, with the following characteristics:

P/N 23-753A9 (stamped 753A9 on the package):
	This ROM *only* works with the M7846 RX11 controller and RX01 drives (or
	RX02 drives with their configuration switches set for RX01 emulation).
	The RX11 is a non-DMA controller that only handles single density
	drives.

P/N 23-811A9 (stamped 811A9 on the package):
	This ROM *only* works with the M8256 RX211 controller and RX02 drives.
	The RX211 is a DMA controller that uses RX02 drives and handles single
	or DEC double density 8" floppies.  The RX211 is not software compatible
	with the RX11.
	This ROM will auto density select to read the boot blocks from either
	single or double density floppies, *BUT* if the boot block on a single
	density floppy is written for the RX11 controller the boot as a whole
	will fail.

I'm almost certain that your single density RT11 floppies will only work with
an RX11 controller.  If you have an RX211 you'll need at least the RT11 system
diskette on RX02 media.  Alternatively, if you have an RX11 controller I can 
tell you how to configure your RX02 drives as RX01's.
	
