If the code is copyrighted, as almost all code is, no amount of change
will let you call it your own.  Anything you produce starting with that
code is a "derived work" and is the property of the owner of the
original; you have no rights to it.

The only way to make code that you can call your own is to start from
scratch or to start with public domain code.

